Falsifies `byte_glob::verification::no_magic_means_the_pattern_is_its_own_only_match`.

The defect: `literal` copies the pattern byte at the escape rather than the byte the escape names, so `\*`
comes out as a backslash while the matcher still treats it as `*`.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(matches_with(p, n, Dot::Ordinary), n == lit)`.

